WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:14.366
SuiFleet manages software updates across connected devices.
Publish a release, deploy it to selected devices, and track
installation results. Organize devices into groups to manage
rollouts across your fleet.

2
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:28.848
Your wallet is your secure approval app. Use it to authorize
fleet management changes. The network verifies your approval,
and each device uses its own identity. Your wallet's private key
stays in your wallet.

3
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:48.141
Release details are recorded on Sui, the shared network. Walrus
stores the software files for the retention period you select.
Private releases are encrypted, and Seal checks who may obtain
the keys. Publishing makes a release available for deployment;
installation is a separate step.

4
00:00:49.350 --> 00:01:03.025
Choose a device or group and approve its deployment. Each device
client checks the shared records for updates on its configured
schedule. Devices initiate these connections from your network,
using outbound requests.

5
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:23.663
An eligible device downloads the software, verifies it against
the approved release, and runs your configured installer. Your
platform controls system installation, reboot and recovery.
Devices that reconnect later can retrieve an update while the
deployment remains eligible and the files are available.

6
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:44.996
Each device reports whether installation succeeded or failed.
The console displays those results alongside separately reported
device health. An approved deployment confirms your intent; the
device's installation result confirms execution. Health reports
describe its condition at the time of the sample.

7
00:01:46.200 --> 00:02:03.971
SuiFleet connects your console, shared release records, software
storage and device clients. Begin with a small group, validate
your deployment process, and expand through staged rollouts.
Reliable connectivity, storage availability and a funded network
budget keep the system operating.
